PROPRIETARY SOFTWARE — PROPOSED LICENSE POLICY

Copyright (c) 2026 Nyrava Websites Apps. All rights reserved.

This file records the intended product licensing policy. It is a policy summary,
not a signed customer purchase agreement. Before taking payment, prepare final
customer terms that identify the purchaser, purchase price, permitted use,
support and update scope, and governing law.

PAID CUSTOMER LICENSE

Proposed price: USD $199 for the first 10 paid business licenses, then USD
$299 for each additional business license. The amount charged and any required
taxes must be shown in the actual checkout and final customer terms.

After a one-time purchase and acceptance of the final customer terms, the named
purchasing business receives a non-exclusive, perpetual, non-transferable, and
non-sublicensable right to install, run, configure, and modify the purchased
CRM for its own business and its own products or projects.

The customer may not sell, resell, sublicense, publish, distribute, or provide
the CRM source code or installation package to another party. The customer may
not offer the CRM itself as a hosted or managed service to unaffiliated
businesses without separate written permission. The customer receives a right
to use the software; ownership of the software and source code is not
transferred.

INTERNAL FREE-USE EXCEPTION

Nyrava Websites Apps and the business partner specifically designated in a
separate written authorization from the copyright owner may use the CRM without
a purchase fee for projects each owns or controls. This internal exception is
limited to those designated parties and their own projects. It does not grant
resale, sublicensing, redistribution, or rights to customers or other third
parties. Access to the private GitHub repository is a separate permission and
does not expand these use rights.

SCOPE TO DEFINE IN FINAL CUSTOMER TERMS

The purchase agreement must state whether updates, technical support, number
of installations, employee accounts, contractors, and use in customer-facing
products are included. These items are not promised by this summary.

NO AUTOMATIC LICENSE CHECK

The current application does not verify purchases or enforce license limits.
Until a purchase and activation flow is implemented, these conditions rely on
the written agreement and controlled delivery of the software.

THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

Third-party components are governed by their respective license terms. This
policy does not replace or modify those terms.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW. Any warranty,
support, or liability terms for a purchase must be set out in the final written
agreement.
